    "group": "201-300",
    "title": "Sliding Window Maximum",
    "workload": "generate 8 arrays of 50000 LCG draws once, then 300 punches of the monotonic-deque pass with window k=64. LCG data sits between the degenerate cases (a rising array keeps the deque at length 1, a falling one grows it to k), so the back-pop loop does realistic variable work. Sink is position-weighted so a transposition in the output would show up, not just a changed multiset. NOTE: all lanes use an array/slice plus head cursor rather than a ring buffer or VecDeque; C's deque and output are file-scope statics so it does no allocation where the other three grow dynamically.",
    "sink": "11945225"
  },
